n/math-academy-id "q-320803" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7y=5 \\\\ 2x+3y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $3$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $3$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 7}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
